spans.s:
Vi-kaṅkata is the name of a tree (Flacourtia sapida), often
mentioned in the later Saṃhitās^1 and the Brāhmaṇas.^2
1) Taittirīya Saṃhitā, iii. 5, 7, 3;
vi. 4, 10, 5; Kāṭhaka Saṃhitā, xix. 10;
Maitrāyaṇī Saṃhitā, iii. 1, 9. Cf. Av.
xi. 10, 3.
2) Śatapatha Brāhmaṇa, ii. 2, 4, 10;
v. 2, 4, 18, etc.
Cf. Zimmer, Altindisches Leben, 59.
